// Budapest, Debrecen, Gyor, Kecskemet, Szeged, and Pecs.
//
// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING:
// Hungary is a CONFIDENT DUAL-TRACK market under a CENTRALISED
// PERMISSION model. Since 1 September 2019 the old magantanulo
// status has been replaced by EGYENI MUNKAREND (individual work
// schedule), decided by the Oktatasi Hivatal (Education Office) in
// Budapest — not by school principals. The mechanics, from the OH's
// own guidance and the civil-liberties literature:
// - TEST: the student's individual attributes or special situation
//   (egyeni adottsag, sajatos helyzet) justify it AND it is
//   advantageous for the student's development and the successful
//   continuation/completion of studies. Classic grounds: elite
//   sport, arts, health, living abroad, other justified individual
//   circumstances.
// - GRANTED FOR A FIXED PERIOD (hatarozott ido), renewable — each
//   renewal must be justified afresh.
// - PROCEDURE: active enrolment at the school where the student
//   actually studies is a precondition; application on the OH form
//   via ugyfelkapu or by post (Oktatasi Hivatal, Budapest 1981),
//   DEADLINE 15 JUNE before the school year (later only for newly
//   arising justified circumstances); incomplete files get a
//   completion call (hianypotlas).
// - THE 2021 CONSTITUTIONAL COURT RULING — a genuinely pro-family
//   constraint worth stating: the OH may refuse against the parent's
//   wishes only where egyeni munkarend genuinely does not serve the
//   child's best interests.
// - EFFECT: exemption from ALL compulsory lessons; the parent is
//   responsible for preparation; behaviour and diligence are not
//   graded; the student sits OSZTALYOZO VIZSGA (grading exams) in
//   EVERY subject at HALF-YEAR AND YEAR-END at the school — the
//   half-year sitting can be waived by the director's decision,
//   which is standard for students living abroad (year-end only).
// - THE TWO-STRIKE RULE (softer than Austria's one strike, and say
//   so): if the student twice fails to appear at the osztalyozo
//   vizsga through their own fault, or twice fails the requirements,
//   compulsory education can only be met by school attendance from
//   the following semester.
// - ABROAD RULE: students living abroad continue in the foreign
//   institution under that country's law and meet Hungarian
//   obligations through the osztalyozo vizsga (half-year waivable).
// - PARTIAL ALTERNATIVE: the school director can exempt from
//   specific lessons only, with exams only in those subjects.
// THE WEDGE: tankotelezettseg (compulsory education) ends at 16 —
// the A-Level years (16-18) fall OUTSIDE compulsory education
// entirely, Czech-style. Use it prominently.
// MARKET FLAGSHIP: the auto triangle — Audi Gyor (the world's
// largest engine plant), Mercedes-Benz Kecskemet, BMW Debrecen plus
// the CATL gigafactory — German and international automotive
// families across three cities with thin English-medium provision,
// alongside Budapest's CEE-HQ tier and university cities whose
// medical faculties teach thousands of international students in
// English.
